In React, when you have a reusable component (e.g., an InputField), the label's `for` must match the input's `id`. To avoid collisions, generate a unique ID using a library (`uuid`, `nanoid`) or a simple hook.

```jsx
import { useId } from 'react';
function TextField({ label, ...props }) {
  const id = useId();
  return (
    <>
      <label htmlFor={id}>{label}</label>
      <input id={id} {...props} />
    </>
  );
}
```
`useId` generates a unique, stable ID for each instance.

